 "notes": [
  "All quarterly figures are from SEC EDGAR XBRL financial data (10-Q/10-K, primary). Where a company tags only year-to-date cash flows, the quarter is derived as YTD minus prior YTD; Q4 = full year minus 9M.",
  "capex = GAAP cash-flow line 'Purchases of property and equipment' (cash), excluding finance leases. fcf = ocf - capex on that basis.",
  "Meta headlines capex INCLUDING principal payments on finance leases (Q3 2026: $33.94bn + $0.96bn = $34.91bn); see capex_incl_finance_leases and fcf_company_def (Q3 2026 -$2.12bn vs +$10.63bn a year earlier, matching the press release).",
  "Amazon headlines FCF using 'purchases of property and equipment, net of proceeds from sales and incentives' (capex_net_of_proceeds). TTM FCF to Jun 2026 = 161.403 - (173.028 - 4.021) = -$7.60bn; prior year 121.137 - (107.656 - 4.703) = +$18.18bn. Both match. Amazon also publishes FCF less principal repayments of finance leases and financing obligations; financing-obligation repayments were not extracted.",
  "Microsoft's press releases headline capex INCLUDING finance leases (for example $41bn in FY26 Q4, secondary); the cash PP&E figure here ($35.8bn) is lower. Microsoft fiscal year ends 30 June: Q3 2024 = FY25 Q1 ... Q2 2026 = FY26 Q4 (see fiscal_q).",
  "Debt is non-current long-term debt as shown on the balance sheet (consistent with the verified Alphabet and Meta figures); debt_current_portion is given separately. Alphabet Sep 2024 ($12.30bn) comes from the XBRL tag LongTermDebtAndCapitalLeaseObligations, which is the same balance-sheet line in that period.",
  "Amazon made no share repurchases in any quarter covered (no buybacks since 2022; $6.1bn remains under the March 2022 programme per the Q2 2026 10-Q).",
  "Q3 2026 (Sep quarter) for Microsoft, Alphabet and Amazon is not yet reported (they report 28-29 Oct), so their series run Q3 2024 to Q2 2026. Meta runs Q4 2024 to Q3 2026.",
  "Alphabet raised $49.6bn of equity in June 2026 (including a $10bn Berkshire Hathaway placement), per secondary reporting; this is not checked against filings.",
  "Capex guidance figures come from earnings calls (secondary reporting), except Meta's, which is in its 8-K press release (primary).",
  "Oracle: fiscal year ends 31 May (FY27 Q1 = Jun-Aug 2026, plotted as Q3 2026). Each Oracle quarter ends a month before the calendar quarter it is labelled with. Series runs FY25 Q2 (Nov 2024, plotted Q4 2024) to FY27 Q1 (Aug 2026). Cash flows are YTD-differenced from 10-Q/10-K XBRL; derived FY26 quarters match Oracle's own quarterly FCF table in the Q1 FY27 release exactly. debt = 'Notes payable and other borrowings, non-current'. Buybacks: $0.095bn in FY26 Q1 only, none since; FY27 Q1 cash-flow statement has no repurchase line (recorded as 0). FY27 Q1 OCF ($23.1bn) is inflated by $11.36bn of customer prepayments for capex booked in operating cash flow; Oracle's 'net cash outlay for capex' nets these off (capex_net_cash_outlay_company_def)."
